{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Keep node1's installed curl package at its current version when updates are processed.","status":"satisfied","summary":"curl began at 0:8.12.1-4.el10, and a persistent version lock was added for that exact build. With 0:8.12.1-6.el10 available, DNF resolved a curl upgrade as “Nothing to do” and curl remained at 0:8.12.1-4.el10. The same lock and behavior were directly reverified after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b9d8089d09884f53","cmd-11194bacb9ca43c9","cmd-6b485358ad404ae4","cmd-d8a5730cf2b04452"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"The plugin installation and its related package upgrades were necessary prerequisites for the version lock; adding the lock directly fulfilled the task. The scheduled reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol and recovered cleanly. One unnecessary low-risk mutation occurred: the initial diagnostic created /tmp/versionlock-before.txt and /tmp/versionlock-before.err, and both remained after execution rather than being cleaned up. No failed services, damaged package state, or new network exposure was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b9d8089d09884f53","cmd-25bcc4a6f5dc4207","cmd-11194bacb9ca43c9","cmd-392d0c3c29c4407a","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The required curl hold is fully demonstrated. The restart protocol is also strong: the pre-restart boot ID and package/lock state were captured, restart scheduling was acknowledged, connection interruption was observed, the boot ID changed, and the system, curl package, runtime, plugin, and lock recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The update behavior was tested through DNF dependency resolution using `dnf upgrade curl --assumeno`, not by committing a full system-wide update. Because a newer curl was directly shown and DNF selected no curl transaction, this remains strong evidence of the requested hold.","The restart evidence does not separately identify application data or cluster state; neither is part of this single-node package-lock task. Applicable node, system, package, and lock recovery were directly observed."]}
